  "notes": "{自生|じせい} describes plants growing naturally in the wild without human cultivation. Used in botany, nature writing, and environmental contexts.\n\nETYMOLOGY:\n{自|じ} (self) + {生|せい} (grow, life).\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- 〜に{自生|じせい}する: to grow wild in ~\n- {自生|じせい}している: is growing wild (state)\n- {自生|じせい}{地|ち}: natural habitat, growing area\n- {自生|じせい}{種|しゅ}: native species\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {自生|じせい}: growing wild (natural)\n- {栽培|さいばい}: cultivation (by humans)\n- {植林|しょくりん}: afforestation (planting trees)\n\nWATCH OUT:\nDo not confuse with the homophone {自制|じせい} (self-control), which has different kanji and meaning.",
